@startuml
' House preamble for ArchiMate layer views (stdlib `archimate` 3.2.2). Start from this file,
' edit below the end marker. Layer order (STYLE rule 20): business on top, application in the
' middle, technology at the bottom, each layer a Grouping frame; a relation that runs from a
' lower layer to a higher one is written with the `_Up` variant so the layers stay stacked:
'   Rel_Serving_Up(app, business_process, "serves")   Rel_Realization_Up(node, app, "hosts")
' Elements: Business_Actor, Business_Process, Business_Service, Application_Component,
' Application_Service, Technology_Node, Technology_SystemSoftware. Every relation has a label.
' house-preamble-begin
' Knob LEGEND_FRAME: colour of the thin frame around the legend ("transparent" removes it).
!$LEGEND_FRAME = "#999999"
!theme plain
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam legendBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam legendBorderColor $LEGEND_FRAME
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 70
<style>
root { FontName "Helvetica"; FontSize 12 }
title { FontSize 16 }
</style>
!include <archimate/Archimate>
' The library sets its own line type: set ortho after the include.
skinparam linetype ortho
' house-preamble-end
